 so fail / dropped-run / fail does not reach 2 consecutive breaching datapoints"],"finding":"The retuned bridge_run_failures alarm requires two CONSECUTIVE hourly datapoints to page (evaluation_periods=2, datapoints_to_alarm=2), but the plan's own off-:00 rationale states GitHub's scheduler is best-effort and may delay or DROP runs; a dropped hour publishes no datapoint, and with treat_missing_data=\"notBreaching\" (unchanged) that missing bucket is treated as not-breaching and breaks the consecutive streak — so a sustained failure interleaved with a single scheduler-dropped run would not page. At the prior 40-min cadence (3 fires per 2h) more datapoints per window absorbed a dropped run; hourly with 2-of-2-consecutive is more fragile to exactly the dropped-run case the plan cites as real.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f624affd7cabb320e","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 6 (CloudWatch alarm retune) / infra/terraform/monitoring_bridge.tf","norm_id":"n7dd6f51afb293dba","priority":0.5956,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Bridge fails at hour N (publishes 1), hour N+1 scheduled run is dropped by a contended scheduler (no datapoint), bridge fails again at hour N+2 (publishes 1) — never two consecutive breaching buckets, so the sustained-failure page the alarm exists to produce does not fire"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{